<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel de Carvalho Pais de Andrade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1774">1774</a>–<a href="/years/1855">1855</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel de Carvalho Pais de Andrade was a Brazilian politician from Pernambuco and president of its provincial government. Opposed to the centralising constitution imposed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-i-of-brazil">Emperor Pedro I</a>, he proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-equator">Confederation of the Equator</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/recife">Recife</a> on 2 July 1824. When imperial forces crushed the revolt he escaped abroad, later returning to serve as a senator of the Empire.</p></div>
